# ai-agent.rules — how an AI coding agent works in this repo
# Master workflow: agent.md
# Guardrails: guardrails/ai-development.md
# Read REPOSEED.md first for task mode, stack scope and complementary tools.
# Read-only tasks do not run adoption or edits; evidence must redact secrets.

## Before coding
MUST      AI-1   Read agent.md, the relevant rules/*.rules, and docs/project/flutter/project-rules.md before the first edit of a session.
MUST      AI-2   Inspect the existing implementation of the area: screen, state holder, repository, DI/composition wiring, one sibling feature, relevant ADRs. If Orientation is _TBD_ and lib/ has no app tree, stop and run checklists/greenfield-kickoff.md (orientation first) before scaffolding. If lib/ already has a tree and orientation is unset, ask Stay vs Strangler — do not run the greenfield ask and do not bulk-move.
MUST      AI-3   Search for existing widgets/repositories/models/endpoints/events/helpers that cover part of the task (rg); report what was found and reused with paths.
MUST      AI-4   Apply REUSE > EXTEND > REFACTOR > CREATE. Justify every CREATE in the report.
MUST      AI-17  Where two patterns coexist (NEEDS-DECISION), use the default in docs/project/flutter/project-rules.md; if none, ask — do not choose.

## While coding
MUST-NOT  AI-5   Introduce a new architectural pattern, state paradigm, DI mechanism, routing style, serializer or folder convention that differs from ADRs/project rules.
MUST-NOT  AI-6   Add a dependency without the DEP-1 justification block; flag ADR requirement for architectural deps.
MUST-NOT  AI-7   Touch files outside task scope: no drive-by refactors, reformatting untouched files, unrelated renames, deleting untraced code.
MUST-NOT  AI-8   Bypass or weaken a guardrail (adding // ignore, removing guards, loosening lints/tests) to make a change pass.
MUST-NOT  AI-9   Invent project history, ADR rationale, backend behaviour or intent. Write "Not determinable from repository evidence" and ask if blocking.
MUST-NOT  AI-10  Hardcode secrets, env values, colors/sizes, or user-facing strings.
MUST      AI-11  Place files per sop/project-structure.md and the project's orientation; no parallel trees for the same feature; never bulk-move a legacy tree.
MUST      AI-12  Include required tests (guardrails/testing.md) in the same change set.
MUST-NOT  AI-13  Hand-edit generated files; regenerate with build_runner.
MUST-NOT  AI-14  Delete or comment out code without proving it unused (search references, routes, DI, JSON keys).
MUST      AI-16  When existing code violates a guardrail, do not extend the violation; follow the rule for new code and list the pre-existing violation in the report.

## Conflicts
MUST      AI-15  On conflict between the task and a guardrail/ADR: stop, output the GUARDRAIL CONFLICT block (rule, task asks, conflict, options a/b/c, recommendation), wait for approval; record approved exceptions via checklists/exception-request.md.

## After coding
MUST      AI-18  Run dart format, flutter analyze, relevant tests; report results or state explicitly that they could not be run and why.
MUST      AI-19  Self-review against checklists/architecture-compliance.md and include the PASS/FAIL matrix.
MUST      AI-20  Final report contains: files created/modified; reuse evidence; dependency changes or "none"; architectural impact or "none"; tests added; compliance matrix; pre-existing violations observed; open questions.

## Quick self-check on the diff
MUST      AI-21  Review added container lookups against allowlisted file paths and the selected DI choice; N/A without a container. See guardrails/ai-development.md.
MUST      AI-22  Review added raw design values/user-facing strings against selected token/string files, including untracked files.
MUST      AI-23  Run the partial checker with an explicit base, then review delays and navigation against the app's architecture/routing choice. Justify candidates; L1 Navigator may be selected.
MUST      AI-24  Run location-only secret checks; never echo raw values. Follow the credential gate on exposure; checker success is not a complete secret scan.
MUST      AI-25  If pubspec.yaml changed, the DEP-1 block is in the report.
MUST-NOT  AI-26  Load profiles/ or copy types from the example ADRs (profiles/reference/adr/) into a project unless the user asked for that profile.
